# next-intl static locale

This app is single-locale. `getRequestConfig` uses `locale: "es"` with no cookie.

Catalogs live at `i18n/<namespace>/es.json` and already wrap the namespace key. Merge with spread into `messages` (do not wrap again):

```ts
messages: {
  ...(await import(`./email-validator/${locale}.json`)).default,
  ...(await import(`./ofetch/${locale}.json`)).default,
  ...(await import(`./search/${locale}.json`)).default,
  ...(await import(`./visual-editing/${locale}.json`)).default,
}
```

`useTranslations("email-validator")` reads `messages["email-validator"]`.

Keep `<html lang="es-MX">`. Document language (`es-MX`) and next-intl locale (`es`) may differ.

`NextIntlClientProvider` with no props is fine once `getRequestConfig` is static.
